The genesis of this idea was realizing that glove options are pretty
limited in vanilla.  GoP are good if you can get them in the early
game, but since there is no difference in encumberance or to-hit/to-
damage between 18/** and 25, even my valk is using gauntlets of
dexterity (I'm choosing silver daggers over Mojo).  That this glove is
ideally suited for Monks is all right, I guess, but other wombats
might be able to use them too.

Gauntlets of Striking
* Add "embroidered gloves" to the list of randomized glove appearances
* Add enchantment to hit and to damage for bare-handed combat
* Doubles the chance of a staggering blow (base is 1% per skill level
past unskilled)
* non-metallic
* does not break weaponless conduct



